one creation path so the double-create cannot happen. Pass criteria: a real-suite gate run completes in its documented ~540s with 119 passed and zero 409 setup errors, and a regression test covers init-on-an-existing-namespace.", "files_changed": ["auger.py", "docs/VERBS.md", "tests/test_auger.py"], "foreman_note": "Tick auger-2026-09-23-23-44-51 (foreman-direct on a dispatched worker). ROOT CAUSE PROVEN BY THE FOREMAN BEFORE DISPATCH (3/3 deterministic): POST /api/namespaces returns 201 and creates the directory, but GET /api/namespaces never lists it - measured 133 listed vs 174 dirs on disk, and the fresh namespace was still absent at t+55s. cmd_init used that list as its existence authority, re-POSTed, and the server correctly answered 409 CONFLICT -> SystemExit -> 106 pytest setup errors in ~24s. FIX (commit 7c4e7b7, by worker gpt-5.6-luna@openai-codex): init treats the list as a hint, verifies a listed ns via GET /api/ns/<ns>/tables, and treats a verified 409/CONFLICT as existing; any other non-2xx still raises SystemExit. INDEPENDENT FOREMAN VERIFICATION (7/7): API-create then init -> rc 0, 'existing', 'declared: 14/14 tables'; the list still omitted it (proving the 409 branch was the one taken); a direct duplicate POST still 409s; a genuinely bad namespace name still exits non-zero (no error swallowing); scratch cleanup via the API-backed delete. GATE OF RECORD: pre-commit guard run .gitreins/logs/guard-20260924T001300.065059Z.log (real mode, live arms RAN) = 127 passed in 367s, smoke 21/21, LIVE ARMS ran 2 skipped 0, GATE PASS, ZERO 409 errors; a second full guard reached overall PASS (127 passed in 334s). AUG-036's blocker was exactly this row; the real-suite baseline is healthy again. Judge: gitreins task complete run this tick; Tier-2 evaluator still in flight at close time. CI: gh run on 7c4e7b7 inspected this tick.", "guard_result": "PASS", "id": "AUG-051", "perpetual": false, "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "PM cycle 2026-09-23 \u2014 two same-day real