 {"attempts": 0, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["+method", "+engine"], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-09-23T23:26:02.631396+00:00", "depends_on": [], "detail": {"fingerprint": "da60981a595d94af1b13219bc4341c9e617646879a550968a9868fe3a993c8a5"}, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "id": "AUG-052", "perpetual": null, "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "WHY (found 2026-09-23 while mapping the 'what is missing' list against the board;\nthis is the ONE substantive gap the board did not already carry)\n\ndocs/DESIGN.md section 4, open decision 3 states the intended v0.2 shape:\n\"JEV gives calibrated choice, which is what we want for confidence, but a\nlarge-context model may propose better questions. Proposal for v0.2: a strong model\nproposes candidate questions, JEV scores them (dedupe via already_answered, rank via\nchoice, completeness via score). That splits generation from judgement, which is also\nwhat the skill's own doctrine demands.\"\n\nToday `ask` does not split the two roles. Measured on a live scratch namespace\n(auger-probe-1790205758, 2026-09-23): `ask` returns `next_subject` as a single JEV\n`choice` value (testability, 0.31 \u2014 correctly flagged below the 0.45 threshold),\none `next question` (what_is_the_data, 0.71), and stores ONE question row. There is\nno candidate SET and no generator: the question text comes from the criterion\nsentence map added by AUG-042, not from a model that reasoned about the project.\n\nSo the engine can say WHAT to drill (JEV is good at that) but cannot propose a\nBETTER question than the fixed sentence attached to the criterion \u2014 which is the\nwhole point of splitting generation from judgement.\n\nDELIVERABLE\n- a generation step that takes the thin decisions + the seed + stored context and\n  proposes N candidate questions\n- JEV as the JUDGE over that set: dedupe with `already_answered`, rank with `choice`,\n  score completeness with `score`\n- the stored question row records WHICH model proposed and WHICH scored (provenance,\n  so a weak proposal is visible rather than blamed on JEV)\n- the budget ceiling from AUG-001 still binds the batch size\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- `ask` can return more than one candidate question, each with its provenance\n- an already-answered candidate is dropped by the JEV gate, not by string match\n- the run ceiling still holds and still emits the budget-thin marker\n- the current single-subject path still works when the generator is unavailable\n  (degrades, never refuses)\n\nCOST NOTE: `ask` today costs 3.36e-05 (JEV only). A generator adds one\nlarge-context model call per ask; the row must state the measured delta before\nlanding, not after.", "status": "pending", "title": "DESIGN 4.3 open decision: `ask` takes JEV's single `next_subject` choice \u2014 split generation from judgement so a large-context model proposes candidate questions and JEV dedupes/ranks/scores them", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T23:26:02.631396+00:00"}
 {"attempts": 0, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["+decision", "+ops"], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-09-23T23:26:02.637825+00:00", "depends_on": [], "detail": {"fingerprint": "22c97e1afafa701005b665f79616747d61b10b30e8d3c7bd4b220408d3e5c114"}, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "id": "AUG-053", "perpetual": null, "priority": "P3", "reasoning": "WHY (same sweep as AUG-052 \u2014 the decision currently lives only in a doc)\n\ndocs/DESIGN.md section 4, open decision 2: \"v0.1 is Python (stdlib only) so the loop\ncould be proven the same day. The fleet convention for durable daemons is a single Go\nbinary + systemd + a loopback port. Recommend: keep Python while the shape is moving,\nport once the verbs stop changing.\"\n\nMeasured facts that make this decidable rather than theoretical:\n- auger is 4,200+ lines of stdlib-only Python and `auger` is NOT on PATH; it runs as\n  `python3 auger.py` from the clone.\n- 13 verbs and 14 tables are now stable; several verbs are still moving (AUG-019\n  write paths, AUG-029 bundles, AUG-005 export).\n- everything auger needs at runtime is a CLI invocation, not a resident process \u2014\n  so the systemd/daemon argument applies only if the feedback loop is ever run\n  unattended (which is exactly the AUG-001 governor question).\n\nDELIVERABLE: a recorded decision with its TRIGGER, not a code change. Either\n(a) stay Python \u2014 and say what would force the port, or (b) scope the port as its own\nrow with the verbs frozen and the substrate HTTP API as the boundary.\nDo NOT start a port before the verb surface stops changing; DESIGN says so explicitly.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- the decision and its trigger condition are on the board (this row closes with the\n  decision text, not a commit)\n- if the answer is \"port\", a follow-up row exists naming the frozen verb list\n- no code change ships under this row", "status": "pending", "title": "DESIGN 4.2 open decision on the record: v0.1 is Python stdlib-only \u2014 decide whether 'v1 proper' ports to a single Go binary (the fleet daemon convention) or stays Python", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T23:26:02.637825+00:00"}
